OK, further delving gives me this...

"NetHack is Copyright 1985-2003 by Stichting Mathematisch Centrum and
M. Stephenson. See our license for details."

A few people I've spoken to believe this comes under trademark law - if
the names (and NetHack) are trademarked, then I have no right to use
them without those people's permission.

If the names of the original artifacts, and the name of NetHack itself
(Eye of the Aethiopica, for example) are not trademarked then I can do
what I wish, though it would be *very* rude to do it without
permission.

Since I'm not using any code from NetHack at all, the GPL doesn't enter
into this - it comes down to whether or not NetHack and/or any of its
components are trademarked.

However, I'm not going to sell the calendar without the devteam's
permission, regardless of whether or not I could technically do so. If
permission is denied, I'll probably just make a freely downloadable PDF
calendar with the images included that way.

So what I need really, is a yes or a no from the devteam :)

